            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nAlthough I do understand the reasoning, the current 'mini.jump' approach to its mappings is the one I'd like to maintain. The reason is that usages of `nN` and `fFtT` are somewhat different. The first gets defined the direction by some other action (`/`, `?`. `*`, `#`, `v:searchforward`, etc.) and pressing `nN` indeed acts as \"along or in reverse of what was defined\". The second one acts as both search initiator and iterator (`fe` - `f` - `f`), so repeating the search *does* (at least subjectively) feel more organic here. Otherwise it is `Fe` - `f` - `f`, which feels awkward.\n\nAs I would like to avoid adding a config for something I don't personally like, I am afraid this is not planned.\n\n---\n\n> ... because the direction of the repeats with `fFtT` did not feel as natural for the reason mentioned.\n\nMy genuine suggestion would be try to get used to this. Maybe even try to remap `n` and `N` to always act like \"forward\" and \"backward\" (some like it, but I don't).",
